paired Ezer the son of Jeshua, the ruler of Mizpah, another piece over against the going up to the armoury at the turning of the wall.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›After him Baruch the son of Zabbai earnestly repaired the other piece, from the turning of the wall unto the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAfter him repaired Meremoth the son of Urijah the son of Koz another piece, from the door of the house of Eliashib even to the end of the house of Eliashib.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9And after him repaired the priests, the men of the plain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAfter him repaired Benjamin and Hashub over against their house. After him repaired Azariah the son of Maaseiah the son of Ananiah by his house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰After him repaired Binnui the son of Henadad another piece, from the house of Azariah unto the turning of the wall, even unto the corner.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀPalal the son of Uzai, over against the turning of the wall, and the tower which lieth out from the king's high house, that was by the court of the prison. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Moreover the Nethinims dwelt in Ophel, unto the place over against the water gate toward the east, and the tower that lieth out.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAfter them the Tekoites repaired another piece, over against the great tower that lieth out, even unto the wall of Ophel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQFrom above the horse gate repaired the priests, every one over against his house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤tex